 "caveats": [
  "One pass of one 20 arcmin field at a time: a body is searched only while it stays in that field during the pass, and nothing found here has been followed up.",
  "Only the densest window of at most 16 days in each pass is searched, because the straight-line trajectory model drifts by more than half a pixel beyond that; frames outside the window are dropped.",
  "At S/N 7 the real sky gives about as many peaks as the mirrored null search, field by field, so the cut sits at the noise and artefact floor and no peak is a candidate.",
  "The two control fields (Barnard's Star and WISE 0855) gave many more peaks at S/N 7 or above than the blank fields, and their mirrored nulls gave as many. The cause is not established.",
  "Injections are pooled over rate and distance, so holes in the trajectory grid narrower than one flux bin would not show in these curves.",
  "The completeness limits are in flux. Turning them into a distance for a planet also needs the body to move at least 1.5 px within the pass, which caps the distance per field and is not folded into the flux curves.",
  "A vetting classifier trained on these fields did not beat the plain S/N cut on held-out fields, so it is not shipped and does not affect any label."
 ]
